     1	(ns yang.python.antlr.repl
     2	  "The Python ANTLR frontend's REPL lowering (docs/design/yang.antlr.md
     3	   §8.5.6, slice F3). Portable: the parser is JVM-only, but a host that
     4	   holds a CST packet lowers it here.
     5	
     6	   One REPL submission lowers to a program that runs the packet's module body
     7	   against the session's `__main__` namespace: the module object and its
     8	   globals dict live in `sys.modules` (ruling 18), so a name bound by one
     9	   submission is read by the next. `(reset)` rebuilds the VM, and with it the
    10	   runtime state.
    11	
    12	   The bundled prelude defines the runtime in the VM's store and `py/init!`
    13	   allocates its task state; running it twice would discard that state. The
    14	   first lowering of a session therefore carries the prelude and returns the
    15	   session marker `:primed`; later lowerings of the same session omit it. The
    16	   shell keeps the marker (`:frontend-session`) and clears it with the VM.
    17	
    18	   Printed lines and an uncaught exception are rendered by the host
    19	   primitive `py-report` (`report`) and written with the shell's own
    20	   `println`, so they arrive on the output medium in order."
    21	  (:require
    22	    [clojure.string :as str]
    23	    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]
    24	    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]
    25	    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]
    26	    [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]
    27	    [yang.python.antlr.uast :as u]))
